# =============================================================================
# Doctoralia — Complete API Test Suite (MASTER — all roles)
# =============================================================================
# Base: http://localhost:5000
# Auth: JWT Bearer (see AUTH-SUMMARY.md + server/apiTester/*)
# Middleware: server/middleware/authMiddleware.js + roleMiddleware.js
# Controllers: server/controllers/*.js
# Routes: server/routes/*.js   Mounted in server/server.js
#
# HOW TOKEN FLOW WORKS (VS Code REST Client):
#  1. Run a login request in Section 1 (e.g. Admin Login).
#  2. Copy the "token" value from the response body.
#  3. Paste it into the @adminToken / @doctorToken / @patientToken / @staffToken
#     variable at the top of this file.
#  4. Every protected request below already sends:
#       Authorization: Bearer {{roleToken}}
#  Alternative (REST Client — request variable):
#     # @name adminLogin
#     POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/login ...
#     Then use: Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}
#
# SUMMARY TABLE — see AUTH-SUMMARY.md for full matrix
#  Total endpoints: 103 (Protected 62 / Public 41) — +3 Home: GET /api/patients/doctors/looking-for-staff (public, DEPRECATED) + GET /api/patients/staff-required (public, generic {staff_required}) + GET /api/admin/public-contact (public); POST /appointments now protected (was public)
#  Department APIs: GET /api/departments (Public, active-only) + POST/PUT/DELETE (🔒 admin)
#  Doctor Registration: POST /api/doctors/apply (Public, multipart)
#
# SEPARATE ROLE FILES (NEW — per your request "all admin/doctor/patient/staff separately"):
#  server/apiTester/admin.http   — 32 blocks — all admin operations (auth, dashboard, approval, departments, complaints)
#  server/apiTester/doctor.http  — 37 blocks — all doctor operations (apply/login, profile, appointments, prescriptions, referrals, schedules window 1:30-12:00 today→Dec31, staff assignment)
#  server/apiTester/patient.http — 30 blocks — all patient operations (register/login, browsing, appointments/payments, complaints, prescriptions/referrals) — +2 staff-required (2.13, 2.14)
#  server/apiTester/staff.http   — 22 blocks — all staff operations (apply/login, profile/assignment, appointments approve/reject, complaints)
#  Each file is self-contained with its own @baseUrl + @*Token + login → 121 blocks total across 4 files (master remains 118 blocks, fully compatible)
#
# FRONTEND AUTH (no new API route — JWT reuse, 1d expiry unchanged):
#  - Auto logout 5m: client/src/hooks/useInactivityLogout.js + 4 dashboards; manual verify: login → idle 5m (or set 10s for test) → check localStorage token cleared + redirect + banner "You have been logged out due to inactivity." on login page.
#  - Already logged in: any login page with token → shows "You are already logged in. Please logout first." + Logout button (clears all roles+token). Manual verify: login → visit same/other login page → expect block.
#  - Protected routes: client/src/components/ProtectedRoute.jsx + App.jsx wraps dashboards; without token → Navigate to /login|/doctor-login etc.; public pages (/, /login, dept/doctor browsing) stay public. Verify: unauthenticated GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/dashboard/stats without Authorization → 401 {No token provided} (see blocks below), and visiting /admin-dashboard without token → redirect to /login.
# =============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
# --- PASTE TOKENS AFTER LOGIN (or use @name capture shown in login blocks) ---
@adminToken = PASTE_ADMIN_JWT_HERE
@doctorToken = PASTE_DOCTOR_JWT_HERE
@patientToken = PASTE_PATIENT_JWT_HERE
@staffToken = PASTE_STAFF_JWT_HERE

# =============================================================================
# 0. HEALTH / INFRA  — Public  (server/server.js)
# =============================================================================

### 0.1 Root — sanity check — Public
# Expected 200: { "message": "Doctoralia backend is running" }
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### 0.2 Test DB connection — Public
# Expected 200: { "message": "Database connection successful", "database": "doctoralia_moriom", "time": "..." }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test-db

# =============================================================================
# 1. AUTHENTICATION — Token Acquisition (run these FIRST)
# =============================================================================
# Each login returns: { "message": "...", "token": "eyJ...", "<role>": { "<id>": 1, ... } }
# Copy the token into the @*Token variable above, OR rely on @name capture + {{req.response.body.token}}.
# Token is JWT signed with JWT_SECRET (server/.env: JWT_SECRET), expiresIn "1d", payload { <role>_id, role }.
# All protected routes require:  Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
# =============================================================================

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1A. ADMIN AUTH — server/routes/adminRoutes.js + server/controllers/adminController.js
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1A.1 Admin — Check registration status — Public
# GET /api/admin/status — always public; tells UI if registration is open (singleton guard).
# Expected 200: { "closed": true|false, "count": 1, "message": "..." }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/status

### 1A.2 Admin — Register — Public (singleton: only 1 admin allowed — "sara")
# POST /api/admin/register — Public — becomes 403 after first admin exists (adminController.js:14).
# Expected 201: { "message": "Admin registration successful.", "admin": { "admin_id", "full_name", "email", "phone_number" } }
# Expected 403: { "message": "Admin registration is disabled..." } if already exists
# Expected 409: duplicate email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "full_name": "Sara Admin",
  "email": "sara@gmail.com",
  "password": "sara123",
  "phone_number": "01700000000"
}

### 1A.3 Admin — Login — Public — ⭐ RETURNS TOKEN (save as {{adminToken}})
# POST /api/admin/login — email is lowercased+trimmed; alias "sara" -> "sara@gmail.com" (adminController.js:95).
# Body: { "email": "sara" | "sara@gmail.com", "password": "sara123" }
# Expected 200: { "message": "Admin login successful.", "token": "eyJ...", "admin": { "admin_id":1, "full_name":"Sara", ... } }
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sara@gmail.com",
  "password": "sara123"
}

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1B. DOCTOR AUTH — server/routes/doctorRoutes.js + server/controllers/doctorController.js
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1B.1 Doctor — Check Departments (for registration dropdown) — Public
# GET /api/departments — Public — used to populate department select before applying.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/departments

### 1B.2 ⭐ Doctor Registration — POST /api/doctors/apply — Public (NO TOKEN) — multipart/form-data
# server/routes/doctorRoutes.js:225 + doctorController.js:5
# Multer: uploads/doctors, field "profile_photo", 5MB, jpeg/jpg/png/webp, stored as /uploads/doctors/<unique>.ext
# Required: department_id (must exist in department table), full_name, email (unique), password, phone_number,
#           qualification, specification, medical_registration_no (unique), new_patient_fee, followup_fee, max_patient_num, profile_photo file
# Expected 201: { "message": "Doctor application successfully submitted. wait for Admin approval.", "doctor": { "doctor_id", ... } }
# Expected 400: missing/invalid department_id  | 404: department not found | 409: email or medical_registration_no already exists
# NOTE: Department APIs are fully included — see Section 2.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/doctors/apply
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary

------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="department_id"

1
------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="full_name"

Dr. Arif Rahman
------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="email"

arif.rahman@example.com
------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="password"

Doctor@123
------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="phone_number"

01710000001
------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="qualification"

MBBS, FCPS (Medicine)
------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="specification"

Cardiology
------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="medical_registration_no"

BMDC-2026-0001
------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="new_patient_fee"

800
------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="followup_fee"

500
------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="max_patient_num"

20
------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="profile_photo"; filename="doctor.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./server/uploads/doctors/doctor.jpg
------WebKitFormBoundary--

### 1B.3 Doctor — Login — Public — ⭐ RETURNS TOKEN (save as {{doctorToken}})
# POST /api/doctors/login — checks approval_status (pending 403, rejected 403) + clears expired suspended_until + active suspension 403.
# Body: { "email", "password" }  -> jwt { doctor_id, role:"doctor" }
# Expected 200: { "message": "Doctor login successful.", "token": "eyJ...", "doctor": { "doctor_id", "full_name", ... } }
# @name doctorLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/doctors/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "arif.rahman@example.com",
  "password": "Doctor@123"
}

